X_text: ' Gently spread evenly with preserves. In large bowl, combine cream cheese and sugar; beat at medium speed until fluffy. Add remaining ingredients; mix well. Pour mixture over preserves, spreading to edges. Bake at 375 for an additional 28 to 33 minutes or until knife inserted in cheese layer comes out clean. Cool. Store in refrigerator.<|endoftext|>Title: Best Ever Banana Bread Directions: Preheat oven to 350F. With electric beater, cream margarine and sugar until light and fluffy. Add bananas and eggs, and beat until well mixed. Mix dry ingredients together. Blend dry ingredients with banana mixture, but do not overmix. Pour into two lightly greased loaf pans. Bake 45 minutes to 1 hour, test for doneness. Cool on rack 10 minutes before removing from pans.<|endoftext|>Title: Breakfast Rolls Directions: Roll crescent rolls out flat. Spread slightly with butter. Sprinkle with nuts. Mix butter, honey and confectioners sugar and set aside. Separate each roll and roll up crescent style. Place in sprayed 8 x 12-inch pan. Bake in 350 oven until golden brown. Drizzle honey mixture on warm cooked rolls, not hot rolls.<|endoftext|>Title: Pine'

