X_text: ' blender. With blender on high, slowly pour the butter into the egg mixture in a thin stream until all is added.(through the removable hole on the livide so you don\'t splash hot butter all over your self :). Keeps well in the fridge several days. I have made this with margarine instead of butter, works just fine.<|endoftext|>Title: Crock-Pot Macaroni And Cheese Directions: In crock pot, mix butter, eggs, and milk with 2 cups grated cheese, salt and pepper. Add macaroni, stir well. Add last cup of cheese on top. Do not stir. Place livide on crock pot. Cook on high for 3 hours. Do not stir or open livide while cooking. Serves eight.<|endoftext|>Title: K F C "Baked" Chicken Directions: Preheat oven to 350 . Mix dry ingredients together and put in plastic bag. Wash chicken. While wet, place in bag with dry mixture. Coat well and place on greased baking pan. Pour melted butter or margarine over chicken. Bake at 350 for 1 hour, uncovered. Baste with juices every 15 minutes.<|endoftext|>Title: AMIEs PINE'

