X_text: 'spice. Fill baking dish around custard cups with water to a a depth of 1". Bake for 30-45 minutes, or until a knife inserted near the center of each cup comes out clean. Remove cups from water. Cool slightly on a rack before serving.<|endoftext|>Title: Tea Cake Directions: Mix sugar, eggs, vanilla, lemon extract and butter; sift flour and add to mixture. Mix well to form a firm dough (some flour differs in texture, so you may need to add additional sifted flour to form firm dough). Roll dough in waxed paper and refrigerate until firm. Cut dough into round slices and place on wilookie sheet. Bake at 350 for 8 to 10 minutes.<|endoftext|>Title: Pasta Salad Directions: Cook pasta to slightly firm and let cool slightly. Mix vegetables and seasoning together and then add to pasta. Toss together, then add dressing. Toss until everything is coated with dressing. Put in the refrigerator overnight.<|endoftext|>Title: Dee\'s Beef n Cheezey Empanadas Directions: on medium heat, add oil and saute onions, red peppers, garlic, and olives season the beef with the adobo before you cook it'

