X_text: ' months. Note: You can assemble and freeze without cooking and cook on the day to be eaten! To serve, defrost overnight and then bake at 350F until warmed through, or bake from frozen for 1 hour and a half. Note: you can also microwave individual servings!<|endoftext|>Title: Coconut Butter Chicken Directions: Heat butter in sauce pan to medium. Add ginger, onion and garlic to pan. Cook until golden brown. Add chicken, turn occasionally. Cook 2 minutes. Add salt, pepper, tumeric and garam masala. Cook 5 minutes. Add chili peppers and cashews. Cook 5 minutes. Add coconut cream, stir well. Cook 2-3 minutes. Finish with cilantro, serve with rice.<|endoftext|>Title: Potato Salad Directions: Boil potatoes for about 10 minutes, until soft but not mushy. Cool. Add vinegar and oil. Place in refrigerator until cold. Add celery, onion, eggs, dill. Add mayonnaise to taste. Add salt & pepper to taste.<|endoftext|>Title: Rice Pie Directions: Combine tomato juice, broth, butter and salt in large saucepan. Bring to full boil. Add rice, cover and cook until liquid'

