X_text: " or larger) brown sausage links using medium heat. Once all cruink are browned, add sauce, puree and whole tomatoes (cut up tomatoes as you add them to sauce). Add chopped peppers, diced onions and sliced mushrooms. Add all spices and stir. Bring sauce to a boil with medium heat. Reduce heat to simmer, cover sauce and cook on very low heat 2 to 3 hours. Stir occasionally to ensure sauce does not stick to bottom of pot. Serve over pasta with Italian garlic bread and grated Parmesan cheese. Can be used in any Italian or sauce dish. Great as pizza sauce, too. Leftover sauce can be frozen up to 6 months. Sauce taste gets better each time it's served.<|endoftext|>Title: Roasted Sweet Potatoes with Fresh Marjoram Directions: Preheat oven to 450F. Toss sweet potatoes with oil and marjoram in large bowl. Spread sweet potatoes in single layer on 2 baking sheets. Place 1 sprig marjoram atop sweet potatoes on each baking sheet; set 1 sheet on top oven rack and 1 sheet on bottom rack. Roast sweet potatoes 10 minutes. Stir, switch position of baking sheets on oven racks, and roast 5 minutes more. Stir sweet potatoes"

