X_text: " the freezer for 10 minutes or so. Meanwhile, chop the chestnuts and heat the butter on a low heat. Once the butter is hot, add the sage leaves and chestnuts and fry for a couple of minutes. Also get a saucepan of boiling salted water on the go. Once water is boiling add the ravioli to the water and cook until al dente — with fresh pasta it shouldn't take more than 5 minutes, more like 3. Then serve with the butter drizzled over and perhaps a peppery rocket salad. Make a mound of flour on a large surface. Make a deep well in the middle of the flour and crack the 4 eggs into the centre. Whisk the eggs with a fork, gradually bringing in a little bit of flour. You may need to add a bittachment of cold water too as you bring the dough together. Slowly the dough should become soft and pliable but not sticky. If sticky, add a bit more flour, or if too dry, add a touch of water. Livide the dough into four pieces, wrap in cling film or tea towels and refrigerate for about an hour or until needed. The pasta will last a few days refrigerated.<|endoftext|>Title: Easy BAK"

