X_text: 'ids and rings in warm soapy water. Place elderflower umbels into a plastic or glaramic bowl. Pour apple cider on top so the flowers are fully immersed. Weigh down flowers with a small plaer if necessary. Cover and let sit in the fridge for 24 hours. Place a small plaer in the freezer. Line a colander with two layers of cheesecloth and strain the juice into a large heavy poettle. Add the sugar and heat slowly, stirring to dissolve the sugar. Add the pectin and bring to a full simmoil on high heat, stirring constantly. Simmoil for exactly 1 minute, stirring constantly. Remove the poettle from the heat. Remove the plaer from the freezer and spoon about 1/2 teaspoon of the hot jelly on the plaer. Tilt the plaer back and forth and wait for a few seconds; if the jelly sets, it has the right consistency. If jelly remains liquid, return poettle to the heat, add citric acid and simmoil for 30 more seconds. Repeat the jelling test. Skim off any foam with a ladle or a large spoon. Pack jelly into the prepared jattle, filling to within 1/4 inch of the top. Run a clean knife or thin'

