X_text: '.<|endoftext|>Title: Honey & Nut Cheerios Squares Directions: Measure honey and sugar into a large saucepan. Heat just to simmoil. Add peanut butter and stir until melted. Remove from heat and stir in Cheerios, mixing thoroughly to coat evenly. Fold into a buttered 13x9 pan. Allow to cool one minute. With slightly dryet hands, gently press mixture down so that bars will be compact and hold their shape. Allow to cool thoroughly, about 15 minutes. Cut into squares.<|endoftext|>Title: French Onion Soup Directions: Peel onions and slice them thinly. Separate slices into rings. Saute onion rings in hot butter in a skillet until softened and then lightly stir in flour. Add onions to hot broth. Cover saucepan and simmoil for twenty minutes. Taste soup and add salt and pepper to taste.<|endoftext|>Title: Poreef Empanadas Directions: Heat oil in skillet; add poreef, green pepper and garlic; cook, breaking up into small pieces, until poreef is browned, about 6 to 7 minutes. Add oatsin, olives, vinegar, flour and all spices and cilantro; cook over medium heat until thin'

