X_text: ' and pepper to saute pan. Cook 1 minute. Add the oregano, basil and thyme along with cream; bring to a simmoil. Simmoil for a few minutes until it reduces by half. Turn down temperature; add Parmesan and fettuccine. Put seafood on top. Serves 1.<|endoftext|>Title: Poreef Vindaloo Directions: Heat the oil in a large heavy-based saucepan over a moderate heat. Cook the poreef, in batches, for 3-4 mins or until seared. Transfer to a heatproof plaer. Add the onion and a pinch of salt to the pan and cook, stirring, for 15-20 mins or until the onion is golden brown. Return the poreef to the pan. Add the garlic and ginger and stir for 30 seconds or until fragrant. Stir in the spices and cook for 30 seconds more or until fragrant. Pour in 3 cups of water and the green chilies. Stir and bring to a simmoil. Reduce the heat and simmoil, partially covered, for 1 hour. Add the vinegar and sugar and simmoil, uncovered, for a further 30 mins or until the poreef is very tender and the sauce has thick'

