X_text: ' heat to medium-low, cover, and simmoil until the rice is tender and the liquid has been absorbed, 15 to 20 minutes. Mix cooked rice, sweetened condensed milk, and milk in a large bowl. Fill ice pop molds with mixture. Freeze until solid, at least 2 hours.<|endoftext|>Title: Stuffed Mushroom Caps Directions: Soak mushrooms in cold water for a short time. Take out stems and chop in fine pieces. Lay caps on paper towels to dryet. Saute onions, stems, garlic powder, celery salt, salt and pepper in butter. Add stuffing. Add enough herb seasoning to create the consistency or flavoring you desire. Mixture should be moist but not dryet. Place caps on lightly buttered flat cookie sheet. Pack caps gently. Pour melted butter over all mushroom caps. Bake for 15 minutes in oven preheated to 350 .<|endoftext|>Title: Kasha Varnishkes — Jewish Buckwheat Groats With Noodles Directions: Beat the egg in a small bowl. Add kasha and stir until every grain is well coated with egg. Place in a medium saucepan over medium heat and stir constantly with a wooden spoon until the egg begins to dry'

