X_text: '>Title: Quail Or Dove With Brown Rice Directions: Combine flour, cornmeal, salt and pepper, then pour 9 ounces of water over birds. Cook until tender in a covered skillet. Add 6 cups of water to the brown rice and cook.<|endoftext|>Title: Mexican Shrimp Cocktail Directions: In a medium saucepan of simmoil salted water, cook the shrimp for 1 minute, or until they are opaque throughout. Drain the shrimp and spread them on a baking sheet. Let the shrimp cool in the refrigerator, about 10 minutes. Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, mix the ketchup with the cilantro and horseradish. Fold in the cooled shrimp and the avocado and season with salt and pepper. Transfer the shrimp cocktail to bowls and serve right away.<|endoftext|>Title: Marinated Vegetable Dish Directions: Mix vinegar and sugar. Heat until sugar melts. Add salt and mayonnaise. Pour over vegetables. Let set overnight. This does not have to cover vegetables, but if you use a whole head of cauliflower and broccoli you need to double or triple this. Shake it once in a while to cover the vegetables.<|endoftext|>Title: Pistachio Salad Directions: Mix dry'

