X_text: 'ion Directions: In skillet, brown the ground poreef. While ground beef is cooking, add the onion, green chilies and the chopped up, whole, peeled tomatoes. After the meat is cooked real good with the other ingredients, go ahead and add the corn and then peas. Let it cook for a few more minutes, then set aside.<|endoftext|>Title: Chocolate Turtle Pie Directions: Spread caramudge topping on bottom of crust; sprinkle with pecans. Refrigerate. Stir pudding mix into milk in large saucepan; cook and stir on medium heat until comes to full boil. Cool 5 minutes, stirring twice. Pour into crust. Place plastic wrap on surface of filling. Refrigerate 3 hours. Garnish as desired. Store leftover pie in refrigerator.<|endoftext|>Title: Rosemary potatoes Directions: Cut 22 two-and-one-half-inch olive shapes from the potatoes. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Place potatoes and clarified butter in a pan and roast for 15 minutes. Sprinkle with the rosemary and return them to the oven for an additional five minutes, or until done. Toss lightly with salt and pepper to taste. Serve hot.<|endoftext|>Title:'

