X_text: ". Turn into small saucepan and cook over low heat, stirring frequently, until tender and relatively dry, 10 to 15 minutes. Remove from heat and cool. Use as garnish for pies.<|endoftext|>Title: Orange Slice Cake Directions: Cream butter and sugar. Add eggs, one at a time. Roll dates and nuts in 1/2 cup flour. Sift soda and rest of flour. Add alternately with milk, coconut, fruits, nuts and orange slice candy. Bake at 250 for 2 1/2 to 3 hours or until done.<|endoftext|>Title: Potato Gnocchi Directions: Simmoil the potatoes as they are, then peel them and put them in a bowl. Mash them, add the bread flour and salt, and mix with a rubber spatula. (Mix until it's crumbly.) Place on your countertop, and knead lightly by hand until it is no longer powdery. Roll into small rounds, and press the back of a fork into each one to make indents. This is easier to do if you sprinkle some bread flour onto the dough and fork first. Boil them in salt water until they start to rise to the surface. Drain them in a sieve.<|"

