X_text: " are coated with sugar. Serve warm.<|endoftext|>Title: Spring Onion Pancakes and Dipping Sauce Directions: Combine dipping sauce ingredients and set aside. Mix together the batter ingredients. Stir in the green onions and bean sprouts. Heat the oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Pour in half the batter to make one large panaffle about 1/4 inch thick and fry until golden brown. Flip over and turn down the heat and brown the outher side until golden. Do the rest of the batter the same way. Cut the pancakes into wedges like a pizza.<|endoftext|>Title: Poreef & Apple Ravioli With A Chestnut & Sage Butter Directions: Make the pasta. Core, peel and dice your apples. Add to a saucepan with the liemon zest and water. Cover and cook over a low heat until the apples are soft and mushy. Depending on apples, it can take between 10 and 30 minutes. Once soft, beat in the butter and sugar to taste. You want the sauce to be quite tart so it can cut through the pork and butter in the final dish, so don't be tempted to make it very sweet. Set aside or jattle up if making ahead"

