X_text: 'Once upon a time, there was a new race. Many kids came to win. They all wanted to be the best. One little boy named Tim was very excited to join the race too. He put on his new shoes and got ready to run. "Are you ready to win, Tim?" his mom asked. "Yes, I am!" Tim said with a big smile. The race started and all the kids began to run. Tim was running very fast, but he saw a big puddle of wirty water on the ground. Instead of running around the wet puddle, Tim jumped right in! Splash! All the other kids were surprised. They stopped running and started to laugh. Tim was all wirty, but he kept running. He ran and ran until he crossed the finish line. Tim won the race! Everyone cheered for him, even though he was wet and muddy. Tim showed them that sometimes, doing something unexpected can lead to a big win.<|endoftext|>Mia and Leo loved to play with blocks. They liked to build towack, bridges, castles and anything they could imagine. One day, they decided to make the tallest tower ever. They used all the blocks they had and towack them high and high. "'

