X_text: 'Look at our towack!" Mia said. "It is so big and charming!" "Yes, it is!" Leo agreed. "But I wonder if we can make it even bigger. Can we ask Mom for more blocks?" Mia nodded. "Let\'s go and ask her. Maybe she has some in the closet." They ran to the kitchen, where Mom was making lunch. They asked her politely if they could have more blocks. Mom smiled and said yes. She told them to wait a minute while she got them from the closet. But while they were waiting, something happened. The cat, who was sleeping on the couch, woke up and saw the tower. He was curious and wanted to play with it. He jumped off the couch and ran to the towack. He pawed at the blocks and knocked them down. The tower fell with a loud crash. Mia and Leo heard the noise and ran back to the living room. They saw the cat and the mess. They felt sad and angry. "Bad cat!" Mia shouted. "You ruined our towack!" "Go away!" Leo cried. "You are not our friend!" The cat looked at them and meowed. He did not understand why they were mad. He just wanted to have fun'

